          "pairingText": "Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, and Riesling are my top picks for Pork Chops. Chardonnay suits simple chops or chops in a butter or cream sauce, dry riesling complements sweet additions like honey mustard or apples, and pinot noir is a safe bet for pork dishes in general. You could try Bench Sonoma Coast Pinot Noir. Reviewers quite like it with a 4.6 out of 5 star rating and a price of about 20 dollars per bottle.",
