      "instructions": "Pick the mint leaves and wash it in running water.\nClean and grate the ginger.\nHeat water in a vessel and add sugar to it. Let the sugar dissolve; filter the sugar syrup with a thin muslin cloth.\nBoil it further on medium heat till the syrup becomes a bit thick, about 20 minutes. Take off heat and cool the syrup.\nNow add the mint leaves, grated ginger and juice of lemons. Leave it aside for 4-5 hours to let the mint flavor seep into the syrup. Add green color if required.\nStore the concentrate in a clean glass bottle.\nTo make the drink, pour about 1 tbsp. of the concentrate and add water to suit your taste.\nTop it with crushed ice and serve the refreshing Minty-lemony drink.",
