      "summary": "Honey Sweet Corn Bread is a <b>lacto ovo vegetarian</b> bread. For <b>18 cents per serving</b>, this recipe <b>covers 4%</b> of your daily requirements of vitamins and minerals. This recipe makes 12 servings with <b>140 calories</b>, <b>3g of protein</b>, and <b>3g of fat</b> each. From preparation to the plate, this recipe takes about <b>45 minutes</b>. A mixture of sugar, butter, milk, and a handful of other ingredients are all it takes to make this recipe so flavorful. 2 people have made this recipe and would make it again. Only a few people really liked this Southern dish. It is brought to you by Foodista. Overall, this recipe earns a <b>rather bad spoonacular score of 19%</b>. <a href=\"https://spoonacular.com/recipes/honey-sweet-corn-bread-1211207\">Honey Sweet Corn Bread</a>, <a href=\"https://spoonacular.com/recipes/honey-corn-bread-395137\">Honey Corn Bread</a>, and <a href=\"https://spoonacular.com/recipes/bread-baking-sweet-corn-yeast-bread-25700\">Bread Baking: Sweet Corn Yeast Bread</a> are very similar to this recipe.",
